---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
import strip from '../assets/coast-strip.jpg';
---
<Base
  title="Who I Work With | Therapy for Immigrants, First-Gen and High-Functioning Adults"
  description="Online therapy in California for immigrants, first-generation adults and high-functioning adults dealing with anxiety, burnout, identity and belonging."
>
  <section class="page-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Who I work with</p>
      <h1>Immigration, first-generation identity, and belonging</h1>
      <p class="lead">Immigration and first-generation experiences often reshape how people relate to family, responsibility, success, and belonging. Many clients find themselves balancing multiple cultural frameworks at once.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="wrap">
    <Image src={strip} alt="" widths={[800, 1280, 1920]} sizes="100vw" quality={70} style="width:100%;aspect-ratio:8/3;object-fit:cover;border-radius:4px" />
  </div>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Immigrants &amp; first-generation adults</p>
        <h2>Common experiences</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <ul>
          <li>Supporting family financially or emotionally from afar</li>
          <li>Managing visa constraints or long-term uncertainty</li>
          <li>Feeling guilt for building a life that looks different from family expectations</li>
          <li>Holding mixed emotions toward family: responsibility, frustration, obligation</li>
          <li>Acting as a bridge between cultures (language, values, expectations)</li>
        </ul>
        <p><a href="/blog/the-silent-survival-mode-of-immigrants-in-america">Read my essay on the silent survival mode of immigrants in America</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Identity</p>
        <h2>How identity shows up</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>Identity conflict often appears as:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Burnout</li>
          <li>Stagnation</li>
          <li>Feeling disconnected from things that once felt meaningful</li>
          <li>Difficulty making decisions</li>
          <li>A sense of being "in between" rather than fully belonging</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">High-functioning adults</p>
        <h2>Holding it together on the outside</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>I work with high-functioning adults who are navigating the complexities of modern life: those dealing with anxiety, burnout, self-doubt, and the weight of always having to "hold it together."</p>
        <p>I specialize in working with people who look fine on the outside but feel disconnected, overwhelmed, or uncertain about their direction internally. Whether you're dealing with imposter syndrome, relationship challenges, life transitions, or cultural identity struggles, my goal is to help you feel truly seen and supported.</p>
        <p>While I specialize in working with immigrants and first-generation individuals, I also work with adults navigating identity, relationships, and life transitions more broadly.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white section--line">
    <div class="wrap cols">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A South Asian therapist</p>
        <h2>My perspective</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="prose">
        <p>As a South Asian therapist and an immigrant myself, I bring a nuanced understanding of cultural identity, migration, and the unique pressures faced by immigrants and first-generation individuals.</p>
        <p>I approach this work with curiosity rather than assumption. Even within similar cultural backgrounds, each person's experience is different.</p>
        <p>Therapy becomes a space to understand how your experiences, values, and environment intersect and how you want to move forward.</p>
        <p><a class="arrow-link" href="/approach">How I work</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand />
</Base>
